From 2e8e6f7718e21e345ae11b08c5474046ff5d364b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zonghan Xu <xzonghan@google.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 03:58:26 -0700
Subject: [Backport] CVE-2026-113040: Improper input validation in Proxy

Manual backport of patch originally reviewed on
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8560657.
Adds the WeakPtrFactory to ConfiguredProxyResolutionRequest that
was added as part of another change, but should work here without problems.

Improve lifetime management in CPRRequest

When an in-flight proxy resolution request fails with
ERR_PAC_SCRIPT_TERMINATED, ConfiguredProxyResolutionService resets its
config and may synchronously re-initialize other pending requests.
During this synchronous re-initialization, a sibling request's callback
can cancel and destroy the completing request while its completion stack
frames are still active.

This change improves request lifetime management:
- End the PROXY_RESOLUTION_SERVICE NetLog event before resetting the
  proxy config in DidFinishResolvingProxy().
- Clear `service_` and `results_` in ConfiguredProxyResolutionRequest
  before calling DidFinishResolvingProxy().
- Guard completion paths with base::WeakPtr to return early if the
  request is destroyed during re-entrant callbacks.

Bug: 568906040
Change-Id: I270e5efe43ebaabc29c8ceead1bae85f3462082d
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8560657
Reviewed-by: Kenichi Ishibashi <bashi@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Zonghan Xu <xzonghan@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1717484}
Reviewed-on: https://codereview.qt-project.org/c/qt/qtwebengine-chromium/+/783205
Reviewed-by: Moss Heim <moss.heim@qt.io>
